<title>UK: Most UK air freight goes as long-haul bellyhold.</title>
<headline>Most UK air freight goes as long-haul bellyhold.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-04-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>Fifty six percent of the UK's air freight last year was carried on scheduled long-haul passenger flights, annual Civil Aviation Authority's (CAA) data shows.</p>
<p>Non-EU scheduled passenger flights carried 1.006 million tonnes of freight whilst an additional 188,000 tonnes was carried to European Union countries on scheduled passenger flights out of total UK freight for last year of 1.783 million tonnes.</p>
<p>Scheduled cargo flights lifted 189,000 to non-EU destinations and 42 tonnes to the EU. Charter cargo aircraft were the third largest category lifting 144,000 tonnes to EU destinations and 70 tonnes to other international destinations.</p>
